# tabscreen: non-root USB access to the Android tablet, at both stages of
# the AOA handshake (docs/wire-protocol.md, host/src/aoa.rs).
#
# Confirmed live (2026-08-20) that once a device is already in accessory
# mode from a prior session, the host daemon doesn't strictly need root --
# but a *fresh* handshake (SEND_STRING/START_ACCESSORY control transfers)
# does need write access to the device's control endpoint, which requires
# either root or this rule. TAG+="uaccess" grants access to whichever user
# owns the active graphical seat (systemd-logind), which is the right
# model for a single-user desktop -- GROUP="plugdev"/MODE are kept
# alongside it as a fallback for systems where uaccess isn't in effect.
#
# Two vendor/product matches, matching host/src/aoa.rs exactly:
#   - 339b (HONOR, this project's target tablet) at any product ID: the
#     device's *native* identity, before accessory mode is negotiated.
#   - 18d1 (Google), product 2d00 or 2d01: the device's identity *after*
#     re-enumerating in accessory mode (2d01 = accessory+ADB, seen when
#     ADB is also enabled -- both are handled identically here and in
#     aoa.rs's own ACCESSORY_PIDS list).
#
# Update the 339b line (or add another) if this is ever used with a
# non-HONOR tablet -- this project has only ever targeted one specific
# device (CLAUDE.md's target scope, ADR 0004).

SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="339b", MODE="0660", GROUP="plugdev", TAG+="uaccess"
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="18d1", ATTR{idProduct}=="2d00", MODE="0660", GROUP="plugdev", TAG+="uaccess"
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="18d1", ATTR{idProduct}=="2d01", MODE="0660", GROUP="plugdev", TAG+="uaccess"
